* AD8237 Instrumentation Amplifier Circuit

* Power Supplies (Single 5V supply)
Vdd VDD 0 5
Vss VSS 0 0

* Reference voltage at mid-supply (2.5V)
Vref REF 0 2.5

* Bypass capacitor
C1 VDD 0 0.1u

* Common-mode voltage (2.5V)
Vcm Ncm 0 2.5

* Differential input signal: 20mV amplitude, 1kHz
Vin IN 0 SINE(0 20m 1k)

* VCVS to convert single-ended IN to a true differential input centered at Vcm
* V(INP) - V(INM) = V(IN)
E1 INP Ncm IN 0 0.5
E2 Ncm INM IN 0 0.5

* Gain setting resistors
* For AD8237, Gain = 1 + (R2 / R1)
* Target Gain = 10 V/V -> R2/R1 = 9
R2 OUT FB 9k
R1 FB REF 1k

* AD8237 Amplifier instance
* Pin order: BW, -IN, +IN, -VS, REF, OUT, FB, +VS
* BW pin is tied to VDD for high bandwidth mode
X1 VDD INM INP VSS REF OUT FB VDD AD8237

* Load resistor
Rl OUT 0 100k

* Transient analysis to allow the circuit to settle and measure gain
.tran 0 10m 0 1u

* Measure peak-to-peak voltages after 2ms of settling time
.meas tran Vout_pp PP V(OUT) from=2m to=10m
.meas tran Vin_pp PP V(IN) from=2m to=10m

* Calculate gain in dB
.meas tran gain_db param 20*log10(Vout_pp/Vin_pp)

.end
